+## D3. Automatic daily posting (Stage 3.7 phase B — ACTUAL implementation)
+
+**How it works (as implemented, not hypothetical):**
+
+- `devvit.json` registers ONE configuration-managed recurring task:
+
+  ```json
+  "scheduler": {
+    "tasks": {
+      "daily-post": { "endpoint": "/internal/scheduler/daily-post", "cron": "5 0 * * *" }
+    }
+  }
+  ```
+
+  Standard five-part UNIX cron, interpreted in **UTC**: the task fires at
+  **00:05 UTC every day**. No runtime scheduler API is used; registration is
+  the `scheduler.tasks` block above (schema: `config-file.v1.json`,
+  `scheduler` property — verified against `@devvit/shared-types` 0.15.4).
+- The platform POSTs a `TaskRequest {name, data}` to
+  `/internal/scheduler/daily-post` (per `@devvit/scheduler` typings). The
+  endpoint computes the canonical UTC day (`YYYY-MM-DD`) from the server
+  clock, resolves the challenge with the existing `scheduledChallengeIdFor()`
+  helper, and calls `ensureDailyPostForUtcDay()`.
+- `ensureDailyPostForUtcDay(utcDay)` (in `src/server/core/dailyPost.ts`) is
+  the ONLY post-creation path. It is called by the scheduled task, the
+  moderator menu (`/internal/menu/post-create` — the pre-existing
+  "Create Rangefinder challenge post" item, unchanged in devvit.json), and
+  the `on-app-install` trigger. One post maximum per installation and UTC
+  day via an atomic Redis `SET(NX)` claim key
+  `rf:dailypost:{subredditId}:{utcDay}` (TTL 48 h). The post's
+  `postData` carries ONLY `{challengeId, v}` — never the answer.
+- A repeat delivery, a second moderator click, or a moderator click DURING a
+  scheduled run returns the existing post (the menu navigates to it with an
+  "already created" toast); no duplicate is submitted.
+
+**Verifying the task is configured:**
+
+1. `devvit.json` contains the `scheduler.tasks.daily-post` block (above).
+2. In the playtest session, `npx devvit logs -s 30m` around 00:05 UTC shows:
+   `[rangefinder:dailypost] scheduler task "daily-post" firing for UTC day YYYY-MM-DD`
+   followed by `scheduler outcome for YYYY-MM-DD: created|exists …`.
+
+**Confirming the day's post and challenge id:**
+
+- The server log line above names the challenge id and post id.
+- On the post itself: view-source/devtools shows `postData.challengeId`;
+  the client's question is the one mapped by `scheduledChallengeIdFor(day)`
+  in `src/server/challenge.ts` (rotation epoch `2026-11-26`).
+
+**Testing duplicate prevention safely:**
+
+- Invoke the moderator menu item twice for the same UTC day. Expected: the
+  first returns "Rangefinder post for YYYY-MM-DD ready"; the second navigates
+  to the SAME post with "already created — navigating to it". The log shows a
+  single `created` outcome for the day.
+- Menu clicks exercise the exact same `ensureDailyPostForUtcDay()` the cron
+  uses; the cron delivery itself cannot be forced from a dev machine — its
+  redelivery idempotence is covered by unit tests (`dailyPost.test.ts`) and
+  confirmed by observing exactly one post per day over consecutive playtest
+  days.
+
+**Failure behaviour:**
+
+- Post creation fails (Reddit rejects/downtime): the claim key is RELEASED;
+  the next scheduled run or moderator click retries. Nothing is reported as
+  created when it was not.
+- Crash between Reddit accepting the post and persisting its id: the module
+  is **at-most-once, not exactly-once**. Recovery: orphan adoption (the app
+  account's recent posts are enumerated and a post carrying the day's
+  challenge id is adopted); if adoption is unavailable, a stale claim
+  (> 15 min) is released and a replacement post may duplicate the orphaned
+  one. This is cosmetic only — player scoring/stats are keyed by challenge,
+  not post — and is logged loudly, never hidden.
+- A recorded post that Reddit cannot serve (deleted): status `unreachable`;
+  NO automatic recreation (avoids fighting moderator intent); the moderator
+  menu reports the situation instead.
+
